CHAPTER.VERS:
Then the king of Israel called all the elders of the land, and said, Consider, I pray you

          {+}
        , and see how this man seeks mischief: for he sent to me for my wives, and for my sons, and for my silver, and for my gold; and I didn't deny him.

And a man of God came near and spoke to the king of Israel, and said, Thus says Yahweh, Because the Syrians have said, Yahweh is a god of the hills, but he is not a god of the valleys; therefore I will deliver all this great multitude into your hand, and you

          {+}
         will know that I am Yahweh.

Now the men were using magic, and hurried to catch whether it was his mind; and they said, Your brother Ben-hadad. Then he said, Go

          {+}
        , bring him. Then Ben-hadad came forth to him; and he caused him to come up into the chariot.
